| L(s, E × E), Eisenstein | ζ(s)² ζ(s-a) ζ(s+a) / ζ(2s) | CIRCULAR |
| GL(2) Eisenstein L-functions | ζ(s) ζ(s-k+1) | CIRCULAR |
| Selberg zeta of PSL₂(ℤ) | φ(s) = ξ(2s-1)/ξ(2s) | CIRCULAR |
| square-lattice Epstein | 4 ζ(s) L(s, χ₋₄) | CIRCULAR |
| Artin / Aramata–Brauer | ζ_K = ζ · (entire) | CIRCULAR (stronger) |
| totally real Galois fields | contains ζ; families give density only | DEAD |

Any object with ζ as a factor carries every zero of ζ, so its RH is at least as hard; no known object makes
ζ's zeros easier to control by embedding.
